window.TRIAGE_DATA = {"version": "1.0", "description": "Scale Session triage call script (Mariana-led qualification call before the closer's strategy call with John). Each stage has the verbatim script, a clear goal, green-light criteria the rep must hit before moving on, uncertainty triggers, and the exact pushback script.", "stages": [{"id": "opening", "name": "1. Opening", "tone": "Sit back, relax, speak slowly and calmly.", "goal": "Make sure you know WHY they booked the call. NO PAIN = NO MORE TALKING. Don't move on until you know.", "say": ["STANDING MOVES (apply through the WHOLE call): (1) Loop-back every answer — 'hold on, why though?' 5–7 layers, lower tone. (2) Catch hedge-words ('at least', 'hopefully', 'I'd be happy with') the moment you hear one — Level-3 belief flip. (3) Speak from Identity (L4), not Features (L1): 'sounds like you're the type of person who…' (4) Verbal pacing — DROP tone at end of every question. (5) Past-pain probe over future-pace whenever they mention an attempt.", "Hi [name]. Tell me about your day. (If they're busy: 'Oh [name], is now no longer a good time?')", "Fantastic over here!", "I'm Mariana, I oversee and direct the entire social media and content strategy for Lauren's brand. (For context: I've closed multiple 7 figures in cash for Lauren and I've been with her over the last half decade.)", "I have a note in my calendar that you're interested in generating more revenue from your social media.", "So over the next 10-15 minutes of this call, in an ideal world, what are you most hoping to get out of our conversation together?", "(Let them reply.)", "Ok awesome. From our 7 years in this business, we know that alignment is important to a healthy relationship. So this call may feel pretty basic but that doesn't mean it isn't important because we'll go through a few specifics, to see if we can help. Ok?", "If we can help you, I'll let you know, and we'll arrange a second call to go through things in more detail. And if not, I'll aim to point you in the right direction. Is that ok [name]?", "Ok great. So you know we're all about driving revenue from social media. That's what inspired you to want to speak with us, right?", "(If they don't elaborate on WHY they booked: 'Ok gotcha. So that I can understand your situation, what made you want to decide to book this call with us? What problem are you hoping we can solve?')"], "green_light": ["You know the specific reason they booked the call", "There is a clear pain or goal they want help with"], "pushback_triggers": ["idk", "i don't know", "not sure", "just to learn", "just to see", "just curious", "just exploring", "just to find out", "just wanted to chat", "you reached out", "saw an ad", "lauren reached out", "i was just", "think about it", "need to think", "let me think", "gotta think", "have to think", "not sure why i'm here", "no specific reason", "no money", "got no money", "have no money", "no budget", "cant afford", "cant afford it", "dont have the money", "dont have money", "not buying", "im not buying", "im broke", "broke right now", "tight on cash", "what is this", "what's this", "whats this", "what is it", "what's it", "whats it", "not interested", "im not interested", "i'm not interested", "im busy", "i'm busy", "not a good time", "take me off", "remove me"], "pushback_script": "OPENING DEFENSIVE — pick the right branch:\n\n— STALL ('idk' / 'just curious' / 'just to learn' / 'not sure'): 'Got it — and just so I know we're using your time well, what was the SPECIFIC reason you booked this call? Like what's the problem we'd be solving for you?' (Drop your tone at the end. Don't lift.) If they still hedge: 'IDK what you guys do — how did you end up on this call then? Ok cool no worries then, in an ideal world what would you like to get out of this call?'\n\n— 'JUST TO LEARN MORE ABOUT ___': 'Got it, and I can imagine you're quite busy right?' (PAUSE — let them say yes.) Then half laughing with a smile: 'Yeah. And just so we can see what could best help… Do you go around jumping on calls to learn more all day? Or are you here because you're interested in potentially working with us, if you think it could help?'\n\n— MONEY BLURT ('no money' / 'cant afford' / 'no budget' / 'im broke' / 'tight on cash'): 'Oh no worries at all — we haven't even talked numbers, and I don't even know if we're a fit yet. This call is just for me to understand what you're working on. Is that cool?' Then redirect: 'So what made you book this call in the first place?'\n\n— 'WHAT IS THIS' / 'NOT INTERESTED' (weird on a scheduled call — they BOOKED it): 'Wait — you booked the call though, right? So something brought you here. What was that? Even if you're not 100% sure right now, just throw out what was on your mind when you booked.'\n\n— 'IM BUSY' / 'NOT A GOOD TIME': 'Totally — we can keep this tight, 15 min max. Or if now genuinely isn't the right window, want me to send you 2 other times that work better?'\n\n— 'TAKE ME OFF' / 'REMOVE ME': 'Of course — but can I ask, what changed since you booked? Just so I can flag whatever wasn't useful so we don't keep sending the same thing.'\n\nKEY: this is a SCHEDULED call — they showed up, so SOMETHING brought them here. Your job in the opening is to surface that something. NO PAIN = NO MORE TALKING — don't move on until you know WHY they're here."}, {"id": "icp", "name": "2. ICP Check", "tone": "Confident — you've already done your homework on their socials.", "goal": "Confirm they're in our ideal client profile. If obviously ICP from their socials (good audience, real business), don't dive deep here.", "say": ["(Check their socials BEFORE the call. If they're obviously ICP, don't dive deep — just say:)", "So first of all, great work building such a big audience. I saw you have [X] followers on [PLATFORM]. Is that where you drive most of your revenue from? Or is there another platform like email or ads where you're bringing in most of your new clients?", "So I did check your [platform] and noticed [problem — e.g. low engagement, big audience but very few comments].", "(And I know you had a brief conversation with Lauren.)", "Is that the main place you're getting your new clients from? Or do you use something else like YouTube, email, ads, LinkedIn?"], "green_light": ["You know which platform drives their revenue", "You've named the specific gap you noticed on their socials"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'm not really sure", "i haven't really thought", "i don't really track", "depends", "varies", "a bit of everything", "all over"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept 'a bit of everything' here. Pin it down: 'Got it — but if you had to point to the ONE platform that's bringing in the most revenue right now, which one would it be?' You need a clear answer so the closer knows where they're at."}, {"id": "results", "name": "3. Results & Goal", "tone": "Visionary — paint the picture.", "goal": "Clarity that their goal is a good goal and realistic for us to hit (e.g. add a lot of revenue — more than 10k per month additionally — or get speaking gigs from organic). DO NOT MOVE ON until you are certain they have a goal we can help with.", "say": ["Ok, so let's jump 3 years into the future. Lauren, you and I are at your favourite dinner spot, eating your favourite meal, looking back on the last 3 years celebrating our successful collaboration. What are the top 2 or 3 wins we're celebrating together?", "Love it, that's worth celebrating over. And because we're all about driving revenue with social media, just like a personal trainer would need to know your ideal body shape and fitness goals so we have a target, where exactly would you like to get to revenue wise in 1 year from now, and 3 years from now?", "Cool — that's clear. Thank you. So that I can understand your business better, if that's where you want to be… how far off are you right now from that monthly revenue level?", "HEDGE-WORD CATCH: if they say 'at least', 'hopefully', 'I'd be happy with', 'fingers crossed' — catch it now: 'Can I make a suggestion on a word I just heard you say that could be holding US back? You said [that word]. When we focus on getting the [least / just / what we'd be happy with], what do we typically get? And you don't strike me as the type of person who wants the LEAST things in life. Would I be right?... So what do you really want?'", "IDENTITY-SHIFT (set them up mentally to BUY): 'Sounds like you're the type of entrepreneur who never gives up — you've kept going, you're still here trying to find a real solution. Were you born that way or did you have to learn it?' Locks the new identity. Once they own 'I'm the type of person who...', they can't object later without contradicting themselves.", "HIGH-REVENUE NO-PAIN HANDLE: if they're already at a healthy run-rate and downplay pain, don't build from pain — build from unfulfilled DESIRE. 'We never have companies come to us wanting to learn how to sell less — they always want to learn how to sell more. Is that why you came to us?' Then: 'If we came in and did [X], where do you FEEL you could get in 12 months?' (Use 'feel'. Keeps them emotional.) If they lob a humble number: 'OK, 15 — is that your humble goal? You can tell me, we're not posting it on Instagram.'"], "green_light": ["They've named a specific monthly revenue target", "The target is realistic + something we can help with (≥ +10k/mo or speaking gigs from organic)", "You know the gap between current and goal", "Hedge word flipped if one was used", "Identity-shift planted ('you're the type of person who…')"], "pushback_triggers": ["i don't really know", "haven't thought about it", "not sure what i want", "whatever", "just more", "to be successful", "to grow", "more money", "i'd be happy with anything", "see what happens", "at least", "i'd be happy with", "i'd settle for", "hopefully", "fingers crossed", "just trying to", "ideally", "i guess i'd like", "if i could just", "even just", "probably about", "best case"], "pushback_script": "HEDGE-WORD detected — flip it NOW before it caps the rest of the call: 'Can I make a suggestion on a word I just heard you say that could be holding US back? You said [their hedge word]. When we focus on the [least / just / what we'd be happy with], what do we typically get? And you don't come across to me as the type of person who wants the LEAST things in life. Would I be right?... So what do you really want?' Lower your tone, soft delivery. NEVER 'YOU back' — always 'US back'. Never accuse."}, {"id": "revenue", "name": "4. Current Revenue", "tone": "Curious + non-judgemental.", "goal": "Get clear on their current monthly revenue. Doesn't matter what it is — but important we know so the closer can pitch the right level of support.", "say": ["Ok got it, so your monthly revenue over the last 6 months, what has it been exactly? I ask so that I can see which of our levels of support might make the most sense for you.", "ANNUALISED-REVENUE CATCH: if they quote annually ('about $1M/yr', 'half a million annually', 'we do about'), don't accept it — verbatim follow: 'Got it — and just based on last month specifically, what did you do? And the month before?' If monthly < 1/12 of stated annual → it's a one-good-month brag, not a real run-rate. Anchor every downstream conversation off the MONTHLY, not the annual. Pass the real number to the closer."], "green_light": ["You have a specific monthly revenue figure (or a clear range)", "You have a REAL monthly figure (not just an annualised brag)"], "pushback_triggers": ["varies", "depends", "it's complicated", "i'd have to check", "i don't track", "ballpark", "give or take", "around", "a year", "per year", "annually", "i do about", "we do about", "run rate", "arr", "about a million", "about half a million", "around a million", "doing about", "year we did"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept vague here. The closer needs a real number. Push gently: 'Totally get it varies — but over the last 6 months on average, what would you say it's been per month? Doesn't have to be exact, just a real ballpark so I can match you to the right level of support.' Hold for the answer."}, {"id": "past-attempts", "name": "5. Past Attempts", "tone": "Curious — chase what they liked/disliked.", "goal": "List down how they want to get support and pass it to the closer. Doesn't matter what they say but it's important we know.", "say": ["Have you worked with anyone else or any other companies to help with this before?", "(Let them reply.)", "What did you like or dislike about it?", "Thank you for sharing. What attracted you to the Scale Systems way of doing things? What did you like about our method specifically?", "(IF they say they have a coach OR are working with someone else now:)", "Got you, seeing as you're already working with someone else — what's not working as well as it should be that means you're interested in working with us?", "PAST-PAIN PROBE: 'Take me back to the LAST time you tried to fix this — what SPECIFICALLY happened? What did it cost you? How did that feel?' Lower tone, slow pace. Their brain projects 'this will happen again' without you saying it. More powerful than 'what if nothing changes' — emotion is already loaded.", "RE-MEANING: 'You know what's interesting about that? That bad experience didn't BREAK you — it led you HERE. Most people would have quit and gone back to their job after that, but you didn't. You're still here, looking for the right thing.'", "IDENTITY-SHIFT: 'Sounds like you're the type of entrepreneur who never gives up — you tried [their attempt], it didn't work, and you're STILL here trying to find a real solution. Were you born that way or did you have to learn it?' Now they own the identity. From this point forward they can't reasonably object without contradicting who they just said they are.", "PERMISSION RECOVER: '…are you OK with me saying that?' Keeps the content sharp without losing them."], "green_light": ["You know if they've worked with similar companies before", "You know what attracted them to Scale Systems specifically", "If they have a current coach: you know what's not working", "Re-meaning landed ('didn't break you — led you here')", "Identity-shift planted ('type of entrepreneur who never gives up')", "Permission re-licensed ('OK with me saying that?')"], "pushback_triggers": ["no idea", "not sure why", "just thought i'd see", "we just heard", "lauren's posts"], "pushback_script": "If they can't articulate what attracted them to us, that's a soft answer. Push: 'Got it — but specifically, was it the AI content angle, the revenue focus, something Lauren said? Just so I know what most resonated with you.' This helps the closer hit the right angle."}, {"id": "time", "name": "6. Time & Urgency", "tone": "Direct — you're qualifying their commitment.", "goal": "Get clear they have ~1 hour per day and they want help NOW. If they don't, note it for the closer but pass them through anyway — the closer can overcome it.", "say": ["Got it. So how much time do you have to focus on driving revenue into your business per day?", "Right and how soon are you looking to get help with this?", "The reason I ask is that we have a couple of specific offers on right now, so I just want to ensure the timing is good for you to get support from us if we can help. Would there be any obstacles that would prevent you from moving forwards if we felt like it was a fit?"], "green_light": ["You know they have at least 1 hour per day", "They've said they want help now (not 'someday')", "You know any obstacles upfront"], "pushback_triggers": ["no rush", "no hurry", "whenever", "sometime", "we'll see", "depends", "maybe in a few months", "later in the year", "next year", "not in a rush", "no specific timeline", "when's good for you"], "pushback_script": "STALLING on urgency — TWO moves:\n\n(1) INVERSION (mishear the hedge as a no): 'So it sounds like you don't think this will actually work for you?' 9/10 they snap back: 'no no, I do think it'll work.' Lower tone: 'Hold on — why do you think it'll work?' Now they're DEFENDING the buy, not stalling it.\n\n(2) qualifier (only if not financially qualified): 'Got it — and if you were certain this would add decent revenue to your business on a monthly basis, would that change things?'\n\nEven if still stalling, pass through to closer — but make sure the closer KNOWS they aren't rushing."}, {"id": "budget", "name": "7. Budget", "tone": "Anchored + confident. You're not negotiating — you're stating the range.", "goal": "Get a real number from them OR confirm the 2k-6k/month range works. If they give a low number you think they could stretch, run the stretch question.", "say": ["Got it. So your goal of [X] is clear, and I understand you're interested in working with us because of [pain].", "So how much have you set aside to invest in getting this working.", "Most people in your position typically invest between **2k to 6k a month** to see results like you're looking for. Does that align with what you're prepared for?", "STRETCH (if they give a low number but you feel they could do more): 'And if you knew that this would allow you to [insert problems they have], would you be able to stretch that?'", "IF THEY SAY 'I could do that on a payment plan': Get the exact amount they could do. 'Cool, so 1-6k per month wouldn't be an issue for you if you were sure it'd work?'"], "green_light": ["They've confirmed 2k-6k/month aligns OR", "They've given a specific real number you can pass to the closer"], "pushback_triggers": ["i don't really have a budget", "depends what it is", "we'd need to figure", "it depends", "how much is it", "i need to know more", "i can't say", "i don't know", "varies", "what would you suggest", "tell me the price", "i don't have a number", "hard to say", "i'd be happy with", "ideally", "hopefully", "best case", "even just", "at least"], "pushback_script": "Hhhhmmm okay OR Got it — and so we can see which of our options could be feasible, on a monthly basis, what are you willing to invest to be sure you'd get this working?\n\nIf they STILL won't give a number — push once more: 'Just throw out a real number, even if it's a rough one. There's no wrong answer — it just helps me match you to the right tier.' Don't move on without a number you can pass to the closer."}, {"id": "authority", "name": "8. Authority", "tone": "Half laughing on the close — light but pinning it down.", "goal": "Surface every decision-maker now so the closer doesn't get blindsided by a spouse / accountant / business partner objection.", "say": ["Ok thank you. So for your social media, do you have someone on your team who helps with any of this? Like a VA or an appointment setter or something?", "And is there anyone else involved in making decisions when it comes to your business or is that something you have full autonomy over?", "(If they say 'just me' — say this half laughing:)", "Ok got it, so you're not going to hit us with an objection like 'I need to speak to my partner?' or 'I have to run this by my accountant?' right?", "EXTERNAL-VALIDATION REFRAME: 'Can I share something? The brain isn't built to thrive — it's built to keep us SAFE. So when we hit something new and big, the default move is to outsource the decision — talk to your spouse, your accountant, your team. That's the brain trying to protect you. So… what's the part you actually need their input on, vs. what's the part where you're just looking for someone to tell you it's OK to move forward?' Pass the answer to the closer."], "green_light": ["You know who else is in the decision (spouse, partner, accountant, team)", "OR you've pinned down it's just them and they've confirmed no surprise stakeholders"], "pushback_triggers": ["well, i do need to", "i'd probably want to", "i might need to check", "let me think about that", "i'd run it by", "i'd want to talk to", "we make decisions together", "i'd want to consult", "i'd discuss"], "pushback_script": "They just surfaced a hidden decision-maker. Pin it down NOW so the closer isn't ambushed: 'Got it — who specifically, and what would they need to be comfortable with for this to be a yes?' Note it for the closer. A hidden stakeholder kills the close."}, {"id": "fit-qualified", "name": "9a. Fit — Pass to Closer", "tone": "[SLOW + CONFIDENT TONALITY]", "goal": "Book the strategy call with John (closer) and hold them accountable to watching the pre-call doc.", "say": ["Cool. So with what you're looking to do, it's a pretty straightforward problem for us to solve.", "Now I am going to get you to have a 1:1 interview with Lauren's business partner directly, John, to go through the details and specifics on how it'll work for you, to ensure you [overcome the problem they have].", "(*Act like you are looking at a jam-packed calendar with 0 availability*)", "So I'm just looking at John's calendar here… Okk… hmm.. So John's calendar is really full…", "Now, what I can do, because you're looking to work with us… is I can move a few things around for you… Would [X] or [Y] time work best for you? Then I'll be able to get you in directly with Lauren's business partner.", "▸ BOOK THE TIME HERE WITH CLOSER.", "Great — you mentioned earlier that you run decisions by [x], so what's their email address so I can invite them to the next call?", "(Let them reply.)", "Ok great. I am booking that now for you…. [3 seconds]", "You should have received a confirmation email by now, did you get that? (Make sure they check.)", "Ok great so now I'm sending you a document which breaks down our offer and how it works. It's really important you watch that, because when you speak with John he'll be able to break down, for YOU, how this system will work when applied specifically to your business.", "John is really busy — so if you can't go through that before your call with him, can you let me know now? (Get confirmation they can watch it before.)", "Ok great — when are you planning to watch it, so I can check in with you to make sure you've been able to go through it in full, and confirm your call with John?", "Ok cool — I will hold you accountable to that. So expect a call or text from me right around then!", "Just a note, your strategy session will take place on a google meet link, not a phone call. So please make sure you are somewhere quiet, where you can focus. Sounds ok?", "It's been great chatting today — I'll be waiting for your reply to that email confirming you've been through the doc.", "IDENTITY LOCK before hand-off: 'Honestly, sounds like you're the type of person who, once they see something that actually fits, they MOVE on it. Would I be right?' Get the YES. Now when John (the closer) gets them, they've already committed to the identity of 'I'm the kind of person who moves when I see fit' — much harder to stall."], "green_light": ["Strategy call booked + on the calendar", "Confirmation email received + they checked", "They committed to a specific time they'll watch the doc", "They confirmed they can be on a google meet (not phone)"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'll try", "if i have time", "i'll see", "maybe", "i'll do my best", "we'll see how it goes", "i'll get to it", "no promises"], "pushback_script": "They just gave you a soft commitment on watching the doc. Don't accept it. Push: 'John is really busy — so if you can't go through that before your call with him, can you let me know now?' Get a hard yes or move the call. A soft yes here = a no-show or unprepared prospect, which wastes John's time and burns the opportunity."}, {"id": "fit-disqualified", "name": "9b. Fit — Lauren Follow-up (not qualified)", "tone": "Warm — they're not going to John, but Lauren will reach out personally.", "goal": "Pass them to Lauren via DM follow-up. Confirm they're following her on the right platform and they'll be on phone to receive her message.", "say": ["Cool. So with what you're looking to do, it's a pretty straightforward problem for us to solve.", "Now, what I'm going to do for you is, I'll have a conversation with Lauren later today about everything we discussed here, and she'll personally reach out to you to send you the solution that's more aligned with what you're looking to do, which is [X, Y, Z].", "I understand you are more active on [SOCIAL MEDIA PLATFORM], so she'll be reaching out there, just to confirm and make sure you'll get her message — you know that sometimes it can land in the request folder, are you following her there?", "(Let them reply — and make sure you check on your end in case they're lying about it.)", "Okay perfect, could you send her a message now for me? I have a meeting with her right after this call so that way she can check your full profile and reach out to you in a few minutes, to make sure to cover all of your questions before getting you started.", "Lauren checks her DMs a couple of times per day. What times later today could you be on your phone to have a chat with her?"], "green_light": ["Confirmed they follow Lauren on the right platform (you verified)", "They sent Lauren a DM during the call", "They named a time later today they'll be on their phone"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'll follow her later", "i'll find her", "i'll search", "yeah i think so", "probably", "maybe", "i should be"], "pushback_script": "Make them do it NOW — don't let 'I'll do it later' slide. 'Cool — can you follow her right now while we're on, just so I know it's done?' Then verify on your end. People who say they'll do it later don't."}], "uncertainty_globals": {"version": "1.0", "description": "Global uncertainty signals that always fire as a generic PUSH BACK alert, on top of stage-specific triggers.", "signals": ["think about it", "need to think", "let me think", "gotta think", "got to think", "have to think", "got to have a think", "wanna think", "want to think", "gonna think", "let me sleep on it", "sleep on it", "i'll get back to you", "get back to you", "give me some time", "need more time", "need some time", "circle back", "send me the info", "send me a proposal", "send me a brochure", "send me everything", "i'll let you know", "let you know", "we'll see", "tbd", "to be determined", "not right now", "now is not the right time", "bad timing"], "alert": "Generic stall language. Don't move on. Push for specifics: 'Got it — but to be fair to your time, can you give me a clearer answer now so I can either get you to the right next step or save us both the time?' Then re-ask the question of the current section."}, "dm_workflow": {"goal": "Book 3 QUALIFIED sales calls per day, of which 2/week become Accelerator members and 50% of the rest become Skool paying clients.", "stages": [{"id": "dm-opener", "name": "1. Opener", "tone": "Light, fast, casual.", "goal": "Hook them with a low-friction email ask + position you have multiple versions based on stage. Goal is to get their email + their stage in 2 messages.", "say": ["MESSAGE 1: lemme get that to you. what is your best email address?", "MESSAGE 2: and I have a few versions so can you tell me what stage of business you're at? 6 figures, 7+ figures, or just starting out — then I can send over the relevant one.", "ADAPT — drop a quick personal line first based on their bio / what they commented. e.g. 'HipHopTV's vision is cool. Media companies are the way forward. Smart move…' then go into Message 2.", "If you also connected on LinkedIn, slip in: 'Just accepted your connection request also:)'"], "green_light": ["You got their email", "You got their stage of business", "Logged in the CRM for follow-up (in case they ghost)"], "pushback_triggers": ["what document", "what is it", "what's it", "whats it", "what is this", "what's this", "whats this", "what's the doc", "whats the doc", "what link", "what video", "what do you do", "what do you guys do", "tell me more", "no money", "got no money", "have no money", "no budget", "cant afford", "cant afford it", "dont have the money", "dont have money", "not buying", "im not buying", "im broke", "broke right now", "tight on cash", "not interested", "im not interested", "i'm not interested", "im busy", "i'm busy", "not a good time", "take me off", "remove me", "dont message me", "stop messaging"], "pushback_script": "DM DEFENSIVE BLURT — they're trying to make this not-a-DM. Stay light, stay short. DO NOT explain or pitch. A DM 'no' is way less binding than a call 'no' — stay relaxed.\n\n— 'WHAT IS THIS' / 'WHAT IS IT' / 'WHAT'S THE DOC': 'it's a doc that breaks down exactly what we do based on your stage of business. so can you tell me — 6 figures, 7+ figures, or just starting out? then i'll send you the one that fits'\n\n— MONEY BLURT ('no money' / 'cant afford' / 'no budget' / 'not buying' / 'im broke'): 'lol no worries, this isn't even a sales thing — i literally just send a free doc based on stage. you 6 figs, 7+ figs, or just starting out? then i'll send the right one'\n\n— 'NOT INTERESTED' / 'IM NOT INTERESTED': 'all good — quick one before you go, what made you reply in the first place? just trying to flag what we put in front of you that you DIDN'T want, so we don't keep sending it'\n\n— 'REMOVE ME' / 'TAKE ME OFF' / 'STOP MESSAGING': 'totally, i'll make sure that happens. one ask before you go: what made you opt in originally? want to flag what wasn't useful'\n\n— 'IM BUSY' / 'NOT A GOOD TIME': 'no worries, 10-second answer — 6 figs, 7+ figs, or just starting? then i'll send the doc and you can read whenever'\n\nKEY: the 'just a free doc based on stage' line is the universal escape hatch — makes the DM feel zero-stakes. Match their casing / casualness in your reply (lowercase if they're lowercase). Don't justify, don't oversell, don't add to the message."}, {"id": "dm-get-stage", "name": "2. Get Stage (if email-only)", "tone": "Friendly nudge.", "goal": "If they only sent their email and didn't say their stage, loop back with one short line.", "say": ["cool, and what is your stage? 😊", "cool and what is your stage?", "and I have a few versions so can you tell me what stage of business you're at? 6 figures, 7+ figures, or just starting out — then I can send over the relevant one."], "green_light": ["You got their stage (just starting / pre-6 figs / 6 figs / mid 6 figs / 7+ figs)", "Logged in CRM (Message 2 sent)"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'm not sure what stage", "depends what you mean", "ish", "kind of in between", "we just started", "varies"], "pushback_script": "Push gently: 'No worries — just throw out a rough monthly revenue or annual range, even if it's not exact. That way I can match you to the right version.' Get a number, not a vibe."}, {"id": "dm-starting-out", "name": "3a. Response — Starting out / 5 figs", "tone": "Encouraging but direct.", "goal": "Pivot from stage → their stuck point. Give them a list of options to anchor the reply.", "say": ["ok cool, in that case I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you seeing as we've helped 100s and 100s of others start out successfully. what part of it are you the most stuck on? getting leads, getting yourself out there, sales, automations, or something else?"], "green_light": ["You know which part of their business they're stuck on"], "pushback_triggers": ["everything", "all of it", "i don't know where to start", "no idea", "honestly i'm lost"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept 'everything'. Pin one: 'I hear you — but if you HAD to pick the one that hurts the most right now, which would it be? Leads, sales, getting yourself out there, or automations?' One stuck point is enough to book."}, {"id": "dm-pre-6", "name": "3b. Response — not yet at 6 figs", "tone": "Validate the gap between good + traction.", "goal": "Anchor the goood-but-no-traction angle, then ask about their stuck point.", "say": ["ok cool, in that case I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you seeing as we've helped 100s and 100s of others get over that hurdle of being GOOOD at what you do, but lacking the traction to hit 6 figs. what part of it are you the most stuck on? getting leads, getting yourself out there, sales, automations, or something else?"], "green_light": ["You know their specific traction gap (leads / visibility / sales / automations / other)"], "pushback_triggers": ["everything", "all of it", "i don't know", "lots of things"], "pushback_script": "Pin one: 'If you HAD to pick the single biggest thing keeping you from 6 figs, what would it be?' Then go from there."}, {"id": "dm-6-figs", "name": "3c. Response — 6 figs", "tone": "Peer-to-peer, scale conversation.", "goal": "Position the 6→7 figs angle, ask about their specific scale lever.", "say": ["in that case I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you seeing as we've helped 100s and 100s of others start out successfully and scale from 6 to 7 figs. which part do you think you need support on to get from 6 to 7 figs so I can see what we got? client acquisition, automating more, or hiring?", "MID 6 FIGS ADAPT: 'Given your business stage, plus the calibre of clientele you're working with, I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you. What are you currently looking to use LinkedIn for? Getting leads, sales, client retention, finding partners or something else? Then I can see what I may have which might serve you best.'", "HITLIST RULE: any 6 figs+ prospect goes onto the 6-Figures+ Hitlist immediately, regardless of whether they reply. Goal = book a call. Cadence is in the Follow Up stage."], "green_light": ["You know their 6→7 figs lever (acquisition / automation / hiring / other)", "Added to the 6-Figures+ Hitlist"], "pushback_triggers": ["we're doing fine", "not really stuck", "everything's good", "no specific issue"], "pushback_script": "If they're 6 figs and 'doing fine', flip it: 'Got it — so if you could magically fix ONE thing that would make scaling to 7 figs easier, what would it be?' Find the lever even if they downplay."}, {"id": "dm-get-problem", "name": "4. Get Problem → Book Call", "tone": "Move quickly. Goal is the call.", "goal": "Once they name their problem, book the call right away. If they ghost, send a voice memo.", "say": ["oh, well we should find a time to chat for 5 or 10 mins this week. Which day would work?", "we can see how we can help with that in a way that is a no brainer for you"], "green_light": ["Call time confirmed and on the calendar", "OR if they ghosted: voice memo sent"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'm busy", "no time this week", "let me check", "i'll get back", "send me more info first", "what would it cost", "how much", "send me the link"], "pushback_script": "Don't let them push you into more info-dumping. Soft re-anchor: 'totally get it — 5 or 10 mins, just to see if we can help in a way that's a no-brainer for you. would [day] or [day] this week work?' Two specific options force a yes/no. If still ghosting → voice memo."}, {"id": "dm-send-training", "name": "5. Send AI Training (casual)", "tone": "Casual drop, no pitch.", "goal": "Alternative track — drop the AI training link if the call isn't happening yet. Soft soft.", "say": ["Lauren UTM: here's the link for the AI training: https://scalesystems.io/you-ai-start-org?utm_source=Facebook&utm_medium=DMs&utm_campaign=lauren", "Mariana UTM: here's the link for the AI training: https://scalesystems.io/you-ai-start-org?utm_source=Facebook&utm_medium=DMs&utm_campaign=Mariana"], "green_light": ["Link sent with the right UTM (lauren / Mariana)"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback here — casual drop, no commentary."}, {"id": "dm-no-reply", "name": "6. No-Reply Recovery", "tone": "Light, no pressure.", "goal": "Soft re-engage if they've gone silent. One short line.", "say": ["If it's easier you can find a time here: [LINK]"], "green_light": ["Re-engagement message sent"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "If they reply with stall language to this, jump into Follow-Up cadence."}, {"id": "dm-follow-up", "name": "7. Follow Up + Hitlist", "tone": "Personal + genuine. No sales-y.", "goal": "Two parallel cadences. NORMAL list: run the 3-touch weekly hitlist (voice memo -> value-add -> personal feedback). 6-FIGURES+ HITLIST: every 3rd day for 2 weeks with 1:1 value-add follow-up, then once per month indefinitely, PLUS a weekly broadcast email to the separate Hitlist email list. Goal of the hitlist = book a call.", "say": ["NORMAL list — 3-touch weekly hitlist for prospects who DM'd but didn't convert:", "Touch 1 — Voice memo: personal + casual, reference what they said before. Under 30 seconds.", "Touch 2 — Value-add: a video that helps with their specific problem. No ask attached.", "Touch 3 — Personal feedback: one piece of feedback specifically for them (like Lauren did with Pierre). Genuinely useful, not pitchy.", "6-FIGURES+ HITLIST — separate, prioritised list. Goal = book a call.", "1:1 cadence: send a value-add follow-up every 3rd day for the first 2 weeks, then once per month indefinitely until they book or ask to be removed.", "Broadcast cadence: they also go on a SEPARATE weekly email list — one tailored email per week, specific to the hitlist (not the main newsletter).", "Log every touch in the CRM. If they reply with a problem, book the call right away (jump to Get Problem -> Book Call)."], "green_light": ["NORMAL: Touch 1 (voice memo) sent", "NORMAL: Touch 2 (value video) sent", "NORMAL: Touch 3 (personal feedback) sent", "6 FIGS+: scheduled into 1:1 every-3rd-day cadence (2 weeks)", "6 FIGS+: added to weekly hitlist broadcast email list", "All touches logged in CRM"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback — these touches are value-only. If after all 3 they still don't engage, they go cold for now."}], "style_rule": "MIRROR THEIR STYLE every time. If they use capitalisation and proper grammar, you do too. If they use emojis, you do too. If they write lowercase + casual, match that. Match their energy, register, and length. Every DM is personalised to the prospect — the templates are a starting point, not a copy-paste.", "crm_rule": "EVERY prospect you message gets logged in the CRM after Message 1 (so you remember to follow up if they ghost), and again after Message 2. If they're 6 figures or above, ALSO add them to the 6-Figures+ Hitlist (see Follow Up stage for the cadence)."}, "outbound_workflow": {"goal": "Dial leads who opted into our freebies (YOU-AI training etc.) within 24 hours. ONLY goal of the dial = book them onto the Scale Session triage call with Mariana. Do NOT try to qualify or pitch on the dial — the triage call does that.", "style_rule": "Tonality is EVERYTHING. Low-energy, conversational, almost clerical. Whoever wants something MORE loses the frame — be detached: 'I'll take a horse to water, drink it or don't, I have plenty of water.' Short sharp questions ('what got you looking into this?' / 'what do you mean?' / 'why's that?') — never long robot phrasing. BRIDGE every question to the next so it feels like a conversation, not an interrogation. Smile while you dial. When you hear their energy shift, CALL IT OUT — don't just keep going.", "stages": [{"id": "ob-opener", "name": "1. Pattern Interrupt + Disarm", "tone": "Low-energy, conversational. Apologise BEFORE they push back — pre-empt the 'who is this' reflex. The word 'just' downgrades the stakes ('this is JUST Mariana').", "goal": "Get past the first 5 seconds. Disarm them with an apology + the 'just' framing so they don't hang up. They opted into our freebie, that's the only hook you need.", "say": ["Hey, is this [name]? … Yeah, I apologise, [name] — didn't mean to offend you or anything. I know I'm calling you out of the blue.", "This is just [you] over here with Lauren Tickner's team — about the [YOU-AI training / freebie] you grabbed recently. Hopefully that rings a bell.", "(If they say 'I don't remember'): Oh, I apologise — yeah, it's pretty common people don't remember. Looks like it was a couple of [days / weeks] ago. My job is just to get the information out to you — don't shoot the messenger. It'll take 5 minutes here, okay?", ""], "green_light": ["They stayed on the line past the opening apology", "They've acknowledged the opt-in (or accepted the 'don't shoot the messenger' frame)"], "pushback_triggers": ["what's this about", "whats this about", "what is this", "what's this", "whats this", "what is it", "what's it", "whats it", "who is this", "is this a sales call", "i'm busy", "im busy", "i'm not interested", "im not interested", "not interested", "take me off", "remove me", "not a good time", "i don't remember", "dont remember", "no money", "got no money", "have no money", "no budget", "cant afford", "cant afford it", "dont have the money", "dont have money", "not buying", "im not buying", "not buying anything", "im broke", "broke right now", "tight on cash"], "pushback_script": "DEFENSIVE DISARM — they're trying to end the call before it starts. Stay LOW energy. Do NOT push. Whoever wants something MORE loses the frame — so you want LESS.\n\n— MONEY DISARM (if they blurt 'no money' / 'can't afford' / 'no budget' / 'not buying'): 'Oh no problem at all — honestly I don't even know if I can help you yet, this isn't a sales call. They opted into [YOU-AI training / freebie] and my job is just to make sure you got it. Can I take 30 seconds to ask what made you grab it in the first place?'\n\n— 'I DON'T REMEMBER' / 'WHAT IS THIS': 'Yeah, totally fair — it's pretty common people don't remember. Looks like it was a few [days/weeks] ago. My job is just to get the information out to you, don't shoot the messenger. It'll take 5 minutes here, okay?'\n\n— 'I'M BUSY' / 'NOT A GOOD TIME' / 'NOT INTERESTED': 'Totally — I'll keep it to 5 minutes. Quick question — what made you grab the [freebie] when you did? Then I can point you to the right thing.'\n\n— 'TAKE ME OFF' / 'REMOVE ME': 'For sure, no problem — I'll make sure that happens. Before I do, can I ask — what made you opt in originally? Just so I can flag whatever wasn't useful so we don't send the same thing to anyone else.'\n\nKEY PRINCIPLE: the 'just' framing downgrades the stakes ('just 5 minutes', 'I don't even know if I can help'). Stay genuinely relaxed about them hanging up — that's what disarms them. If they keep fighting: repeat the same line in a different word order until they soften."}, {"id": "ob-confirm", "name": "2. Confirm 2 Pieces of Personal Data", "tone": "Matter-of-fact, clerical — like you're a clinic receptionist.", "goal": "This is the LOAD-BEARING move. Confirm 2 specific pieces of data they put on the opt-in form. After they say 'yes' to two of your questions, the hang-up reflex is gone.", "say": ["Just needed to get a couple of things confirmed on our system here, if that's all right with you.", "First thing here, it looks like I've got [piece 1 — e.g. their email / their stage of business / what they wrote in the form]. Is that correct?", "Okay great — and I've got [piece 2 — e.g. their handle / their goal / their location]. Is that right?", "(The exact data depends on what was on the opt-in form — but ALWAYS pick 2 things you can verify and ask about each one separately. Don't lump them.)"], "green_light": ["They've said 'yes' to TWO of your questions"], "pushback_triggers": ["what is this for", "why do you need", "i'm not comfortable", "what's this about"], "pushback_script": "Keep it clerical: 'Totally fair — I'm just making sure I've got the right person matched to the right info on our end. Two quick things and we're done with that part — [piece 1], is that correct?' Then move to the surface question fast. Don't dwell."}, {"id": "ob-surface", "name": "3. Tipping-Point Question", "tone": "Curious, no pressure — short sharp questions only.", "goal": "Get ONE thing in their own words about why they grabbed the freebie. This is the dial's ENTIRE discovery: 'I don't care about a problem. What I want to know is what they're looking for and why.' Don't go deep — the triage call does that.", "say": ["Cool — so what got you looking into this in the first place? Or why did you want the [freebie] specifically?", "(Variant): What caught your attention? What made you reach out in the first place?", "(Variant for a specific freebie): I'm guessing you grabbed the YOU-AI training because you were looking to [insert obvious reason]? Or what were you hoping it would help with specifically?", "(If they give a problem, great. If they give a goal, also great. Don't push for both — pick one and move on.)"], "green_light": ["You have ONE thing they want / one problem they're trying to fix", "You DID NOT go deep into discovery — that's the triage call's job"], "pushback_triggers": ["just curious", "just wanted to see", "no specific reason", "i grab everything", "lauren's stuff is good"], "pushback_script": "Push softly with curiosity: 'Got it — but if you had to point to ONE thing, what specifically caught your eye? Was it the AI angle, the revenue thing, something Lauren said?' Then move on — even a half-answer is enough to bridge to the booking. The dial is NOT the place to dig hard."}, {"id": "ob-book", "name": "4. Book the Triage Call", "tone": "Confident, light time-pressure. You're not asking permission — you're offering a fit-check.", "goal": "Book the Scale Session (triage call with Mariana) NOW. Open loop on how we solve their thing — don't reveal the method. exact mechanic: solvable + excited + time-pressure cover + cliffhanger.", "say": ["The good news is — that's one of the easiest things for us to solve and help with. Honestly, when it's that kind of [thing], it actually makes me really excited for you, because it's usually fairly easy once I understand a bit more.", "What I can do — I actually have a call I need to run to in a sec, I only had a second to reach out to you — but I have [time A] open this week, and [time B] open. Let's just schedule a quick chat with Mariana, who runs our Scale Sessions. What works best?", "(Once they pick a time): Awesome. What's your best email so I can fire over the invite right now while we're on?", "Quick note — it's a Google Meet, not a phone call. So make sure you're somewhere quiet, where you can focus. Sound good?", "(THE OPEN LOOP / CLIFFHANGER): Mariana's the one who'll break down exactly how we'd do [the thing] for you specifically. I don't want to ramble through it now — she'll walk you through it properly on the call. Cool?"], "green_light": ["Time confirmed", "Email confirmed + invite fired", "Google Meet (not phone) confirmed", "Open loop set — they DON'T have the full method, only a hook"], "pushback_triggers": ["let me check my calendar", "i'll get back to you", "i'm not sure i can", "what's the cost", "how much is it", "send me more info first", "send me a link", "maybe next week", "i need to think"], "pushback_script": "FOR PRICE / COST QUESTIONS — verbatim deflection: 'Well, there's a couple of different options. Why don't we do this — Mariana will walk you through the rest of how it works on the call, then she'll show you the options and we'll see which one makes the most sense, okay?'\n\nFOR 'SEND ME MORE INFO' — don't send anything. The call IS the info. 'Totally get it — and to be straight, the Scale Session is just 15-20 minutes, no pitch. Mariana literally walks you through your situation and we see if it makes sense to keep talking. So [time A] or [time B]? Even a tentative slot — you can always move it.'\n\nFOR 'LET ME CHECK MY CALENDAR' — flip to a soft tentative: 'No worries — let's pencil [time A] for now, tentative, and you can shift it if you need to. What's your best email so I can fire the invite over?'\n\nFOR ANY HARD STALL — book a tentative + follow up: 'Cool, can I send you the AI training in the meantime and circle back in a couple of days?' Then onto follow-up (and Hitlist if 6 figs+)."}, {"id": "ob-secure", "name": "5. Downplay + Show-Up Reinforcement", "tone": "Casual, friendly, low-key. You're locking it in without making it feel locked.", "goal": "Make them feel relaxed about the booked time (so they actually show up) + plant a 'I might call you before' anchor so a no-show feels rude. exact moves.", "say": ["Yeah it's no big deal — and hey, if I finish what I'm working on right before that, I might shoot you a quick message 15 minutes beforehand just to make sure you're set. Would that work?", "Okay, and just give me a little bit of leeway the other direction too — if I'm running a couple of minutes late, no stress. Cool?", ""], "green_light": ["They said yes to the leeway / pre-call check", "Calendar invite landed on their end (verify if possible)"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback — this is closing flourish only. Move to wrap-up after."}, {"id": "ob-energy-shift", "name": "6. Mid-Call Energy-Shift Recovery", "tone": "Warm, curious, slightly puzzled — not accusatory.", "goal": "If their energy dropped or you sense them clocking you as a sales call, address it directly. 'When you hear that shift — call it out. Don't just keep going.'", "say": ["Hey, I'm just curious and I apologise if I offended you or anything — I felt like we were having a really good conversation, and a second ago it feels like something shifted. What's going on?", "(Then SHUT UP and let them answer. This often unlocks the real objection.)", "(If they say 'I just realised this is a sales call'): Fair — and I get it. Honestly, this dial is just to see if it's even worth a deeper conversation. If it's not, that's totally fine — you tell me."], "green_light": ["You've named the shift", "They've responded with what's actually going on"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "Not for this stage — this IS the recovery script."}, {"id": "ob-voicemail", "name": "7. Voicemail / No Answer", "tone": "Quick + casual — like leaving a voice note to a friend. Under 20 seconds.", "goal": "Drop a short voicemail that gets a callback. Then immediately follow up on the channel they opted in on (text or DM).", "say": ["Hey [name], it's [you] from Lauren Tickner's team — just saw you grabbed the [freebie], wanted to ask you a quick question about what brought you there. Give me a quick text or call back at [number] when you've got 20 seconds. Cool, talk soon.", "(Then immediately on text / DM): Hey [name] — just left you a quick voicemail re: the [freebie] you grabbed. Couple of seconds when you've got a sec? — [you]", ""], "green_light": ["Voicemail left (under 20 sec)", "Follow-up text/DM sent on the channel they opted in on", "Lead logged in CRM for retry"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback for voicemails."}, {"id": "ob-followup", "name": "8. Outbound Follow-Up Cadence", "tone": "Persistent without nagging. Value > volume.", "goal": "Run the within-hour micro-cadence FIRST, then a multi-day cadence. 6 figs+ goes onto the Hitlist after the multi-day cadence ends.", "say": ["WITHIN-HOUR MICRO-CADENCE: For each lead, dial 3 times in a 1-hour block, spaced 20 minutes apart. ('1 hour, 3 calls — 20 / 20 / 20.') Track your pickup rate by hour in a separate calendar — green = 8%+, yellow = 5-8%, red = <5%. Dial during the green hours.", "MULTI-DAY CADENCE:", "Day 0 — dial + voicemail + text", "Day 2 — re-dial different time. If no answer: short text 'still keen to chat re: the [freebie]?'", "Day 4 — send the AI training link casually via text/DM (no ask)", "Day 7 — final dial + voice memo: 'Hey [name] — couple of attempts, no pressure. If now's not the right time, totally fine — just let me know if you'd rather we circle back in a few weeks.'", "IF 6 FIGURES+ → after Day 7, move them onto the 6-Figures+ Hitlist (every 3rd day for 2 weeks, then once monthly indefinitely, + the weekly hitlist email). Goal = book the triage call.", "EVERY touch logged in CRM."], "green_light": ["Within-hour 20/20/20 attempted on first dial day", "Day 0 / 2 / 4 / 7 touches completed in order", "All logged in CRM", "If 6 figs+: moved onto Hitlist after Day 7"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "Cadence runs regardless of replies. If they reply with a problem, jump straight to Tipping-Point Question -> Book the Triage Call."}]}, "universal_moves": {"loop_back_rule": "After every answer the prospect gives, LOWER your tone and ask 'Hold on — why though?' / 'Why do you feel like that?' / 'Why do you agree?' Go 5–7 layers deep, not 1–2. The first 'why' gets the rehearsed answer. The fifth 'why' gets the truth. If you interject mid-sentence: 'Hold on — what caused you to say that?'", "four_levels_of_persuasion": "ladder. L1 Features/Benefits (where 99% of reps live — never wins big deals). L2 Behaviours ('what does the entrepreneur who makes $2M/yr actually DO?'). L3 Beliefs (catch the words they use — 'at least', 'I think' — and reframe). L4 Identity (people DO who they BELIEVE they are). Speak from L3/L4: 'sounds like you're the type of person who never gives up — were you born that way or did you have to learn it?' Locks the new identity so they can't object without contradicting themselves.", "identity_frame_template": "Universal identity-shift line: 'sounds like you're the type of [entrepreneur / business owner / operator / parent] who [never gives up / always finds a way / actually moves on something when they see it]. Were you born that way, or did you have to learn it?' Use ANYWHERE in the triage — past attempts, results question, urgency stall, fit hand-off. This is the 'set them up mentally to buy' move. Cement the identity early, the rest is downstream.", "hedge_word_catch": "Listen for ceiling-revealing words: 'at least', 'hopefully', 'I'd be happy with', 'I'd settle for', 'fingers crossed', 'just trying to', 'ideally', 'I guess I'd like', 'if I could just', 'even just', 'probably about', 'best case'. The MOMENT you hear one, catch it (verbatim): 'Can I make a suggestion on a word I just heard you say that could be holding US back? You said [their word] — when we focus on getting the [least / just / what we'd be happy with], what do we typically get? And you don't come across to me as the type of person who wants the LEAST things in life. Would I be right?... So what do you really want?'", "permission_recover": "After a sharp move (identity callout, past-pain probe, consequence math), pause and re-license: 'are you OK with me saying that?' Keeps the content sharp without losing them. If they interject your hard question: 'Hold on — you interjected right when I was about to give you an answer you didn't want. Why did you do that?'", "open_vs_closed_gate": "Before any direct frame (the half-laughing authority close, the 'how soon are you looking to get help' question), assess: is the MASK off? Tells = emotional words, personal story, real why behind a number, conceded hidden numbers. If mask OFF → direct moves land. If still ON (surface answers, scripted-sounding) → soften FIRST: 'Sure, no problem. Just so I know — what was it you were wanting to go over in your mind?' that question extracts the real objection sideways.", "verbal_pacing": "Slow down. Drop your tone at the end of every question (don't lift up — that signals uncertainty). This is HOW loop-back works — fast/lifted tone = setter, slow/dropped tone = consultant. 'when your voice lifts at the end they think you're selling them. When it drops, they think you're thinking with them.'", "past_pain_probe": "When they mention any past attempt: 'Take me back to the LAST time you tried to fix this — what SPECIFICALLY happened? What did it cost you?' Past-pain auto-generates future-fear: their brain projects 'this will happen again' without you saying it. More powerful than 'what if nothing changes' because the emotion is already loaded. Then re-meaning: 'You know what's interesting? That didn't break you — it led you HERE.' Then identity-shift: 'sounds like you're the type of entrepreneur who never gives up...'", "annualized_revenue_catch": "If they quote revenue annually ('we do about $1M/yr', 'half a million annually'), don't accept it. Verbatim follow: 'Got it — and just based on last month specifically, what did you do? And the month before?' small biz owners quote 'about $1M/yr' then concede '$40k last month' — the annual is the brag number, the monthly is the real run-rate. Anchor the math to the monthly, otherwise the closer pitches off fiction.", "high_revenue_no_pain": "If they're already at a healthy run-rate and downplay pain: don't build from pain — build from UNFULFILLED DESIRE. Playful disarm first: 'We never have companies come to us wanting to learn how to sell LESS — they always want to learn how to sell MORE. Is that why you came to us?' Then the feel-forward: 'If we came in and did [X], where do you FEEL you could get in 12 months?' (Use the word FEEL — keeps them emotional.) If they lob a humble number, call it: 'OK, 15 — is that your humble goal? You can tell me, we're not posting it on Instagram.'"}, "objections": {"version": "2.0", "description": "The knowledge base for the real-time sales-call assistant. The rep types what the prospect just said; the app fuzzy/semantic-matches it against `triggers`, then surfaces `response_steps` in order. Built from the full Cole Gordon transcript corpus (134 channel videos + 19 hand-processed sources). Every response line is verbatim or near-verbatim from the source material.", "universal_framework": {"rule": "Every objection runs through the same opening before the specific rebuttal: DIFFUSE, then ISOLATE whether it is an UNCERTAINTY objection (a true objection) or a LOGISTIC (money / support / timing). Handle uncertainty FIRST, always.", "funnel_order": ["uncertainty", "financial", "support", "process"], "funnel_order_note": "When more than one objection fires, handle them in this order — uncertainty before any logistic. Timing is a logistic, but Cole reframes it as a priorities/certainty problem, so timing objections live in the uncertainty bucket and are handled as true objections (there is no separate timing bucket). 'process' (prospect taking control) is an app-level call-control bucket outside Cole's 3-bucket objection model — it is handled before the objection phase, not during it.", "step_1_diffuse": "No problem.", "step_2_isolate": "Just so I can stay organized on my end — when you say [their objection], are you more in a 'should I do this' place where you're not even 100% certain this is what you want, or a 'how can I do this' place where you're 100% certain and it's just a matter of logistics? (For a financial objection the isolate is value-vs-budget instead: do you not see the value, or do you want it and it's purely the money?)", "step_3_temp_check": "Money / [objection] aside — how do you feel about the process? Do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [their outcome], that it's 100% going to work, and that now is 100% the right time?", "step_4_scale": "What's really important to me is alignment — we're rolling up the sleeves with you, so what matters is you feel good about the process. Just to be 100% clear — on a scale of one to ten, one being 'I hate this guy, get me off the phone,' ten being 'that's exactly what I need' — where do you fall out exactly? ... What's keeping you from being a nine or a ten?", "step_5_double_tie_down": "So [objection] aside — is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain that this is the right thing and now is the right time? ... So you're 100% in?", "smoke_screen_note": "'I want to think about it' / 'it's too expensive' are usually smoke screens. The job is to turn the intangible objection into a tangible one you can actually handle. If they waffle ('I think so'), that is a NO — cut in playfully and call out the tonality. CRITICAL: a logistic (money / support / timing) handled while uncertainty is still unresolved is itself a smoke screen — if you handle a spouse before doing uncertainty first, you're handling a smoke screen.", "concession_rule": "Never give better terms (a payment plan, an extension, a deposit) for free. Trade every concession for a decision now: 'If I'm willing to do that for you, are you willing to move forward right now?' Going lower again? Also ask for a case study AND a commitment to show up and do the work. People who pay more up front get better results — they burn the boats — so pitch the full price first and use payment terms only as closing leverage.", "loop_back_rule": "After every prospect answer -- lower your tone and ask 'Hold on -- why though?' / 'Why do you feel like that?' / 'Why do you agree?' Go 5-7 LAYERS deep, not one. The first 'why' gets the rehearsed answer; the fifth 'why' gets the truth. Reps quit after 1-2 cycles; the move is to keep looping until they run out of cover and tell themselves the real answer. Different probe for mid-sentence interjection: 'Hold on -- what caused you to say that?' / 'Let me pause you for a moment.' Only interject if pain gap is built and trust is there -- otherwise = steamrolling. (Jeremy Miner / NEPQ -- the universal probe.)", "open_vs_closed_gate": "Before any direct handle (temp-check, scale, double tie-down), assess: is the mask off? Tells = emotional words, personal story, real why behind a number, conceded hidden numbers ('about a million... well, $40k last month'). If mask OFF -> direct frames work. If still ON (surface answers, scripted-sounding objections) -> soften FIRST: 'Sure, no problem. Just so I know what questions you'll have when we talk again -- what was it you were wanting to go over in your mind?' Cole: that question extracts the real objection sideways -- 'I need to see if we have the budget' -- now it's a money objection, not a think-it-over.", "four_levels_of_persuasion": "Jeremy Miner's persuasion ladder. L1 Features/Benefits (where 99% of reps live -- never wins big deals). L2 Behaviors ('what does the entrepreneur who makes $2M/yr actually DO?'). L3 Beliefs (catch the words they use -- 'at least', 'I think' -- and reframe). L4 Identity (people do who they believe they are -- Freud). Pitch from L3/L4: 'sounds like you're the type of person who never gives up -- were you born that way or did you have to learn it?' locks the new identity so they can't object without contradicting themselves.", "permission_recover": "After a sharp directness move (consequence math, identity callout, past-pain probe), pause and re-license: 'are you OK with me saying that?' Keeps the content sharp without losing them. If they interject your hard question: 'hold on -- you interjected right when I was about to give you an answer you didn't want. Why did you do that?' Names avoidance directly instead of letting them route around it.", "operator_mindset": "Cole + Jeremy's license to push: 'I'm not doing this TO them, I'm doing this FOR them — so they overcome their stories and get what they want.' Internally: 'I'm concerned about the CONSEQUENCES if they don't change' — not concerned about closing them. Reps who hold this frame come across as moral authority / fiduciary care. Reps who don't sound combative even when the words are right. Tonality leaks the frame — you can't fake it.", "concerned_tone": "Cole/Jeremy's specific tone variant (distinct from 'lower at end of question'). Same words, two tones: judgmental ('what's the version of you NOW, man?' = broy) vs concerned (softer, slower, hand-on-chest energy). PHYSICAL ANCHOR: hand on chest produces the tone — even on audio. You can't fake it from the neck up. DAILY-LIFE DRILL: use concerned tone in non-sales conversation ('how do you mean by stress?' with partner). Builds muscle so it fires automatically.", "negative_identity_close": "Jeremy Miner — AFTER the laddered why-chain ('why? ... why though? ... where do those people end up?'), close the loop with the NEGATIVE identity rejection: 'you don't sound like the type of person who [wants the bad outcome they just named].' Different from the positive identity-shift ('type of person who never gives up'). This asks them to DISOWN the failure they just described. Pair: ladder why → prospect names the failure → 'you don't sound like the type of person who [that outcome]' → 'so what do you really want?'"}, "situations": [{"id": "went-quiet", "button": "Went quiet", "label": "Prospect went quiet / one-word answers", "response_steps": ["Call out the silence directly, with warmth: 'Hey — you got quiet on me there. What's going through your head right now?'", "Don't push the close into the silence. Re-engage first: 'Be straight with me — what's really going on? Earlier you said this is what you need. Something shifted — what is it?'", "Once they name it, that's the real objection — handle it through diffuse -> isolate."], "do_not": "Don't keep pitching into a dead line, and don't read silence as a yes. A quiet prospect is the call dying — surface what changed before you do anything else."}, {"id": "flat-energy", "button": "Flat / low energy", "label": "Energy dropped — flat 'yeah', 'sure', 'mm-hm'", "response_steps": ["Name the tonality playfully: 'I can hear the energy dropped a little — and that's totally fine. Let's just be honest with each other: what's really going on?'", "Re-anchor to their own words: 'Earlier you told me [their goal / their pain]. Is that still true? Because right now it doesn't sound 100%.'", "If they waffle, feed them the objection — it's usually nerves: 'It sounds like a bit of nerves — is it?' Then handle nerves."], "do_not": "Don't ignore a flat 'yeah' and treat it as agreement. Flat tonality is a no — surface it now, not after the price drop."}, {"id": "hedging", "button": "Hedging tonality", "label": "Hedging — 'I think so', 'probably', 'we'll see'", "response_steps": ["Cut in playfully and call out the hedge: 'I think so? That doesn't sound 100% certain — so let's just be honest with each other, what's really going on?'", "Push for the real answer: 'Do you 100% think this will work, and do you 100% want to do this? If it's not a clear yes, that's fine — but tell me what's in the way.'", "A hedge is a NO until proven otherwise. Turn the intangible into a tangible objection you can handle."], "do_not": "Don't let a hedge slide into a booked follow-up. 'I think so' is not a yes."}, {"id": "combative", "button": "Got combative", "label": "Prospect is hostile / rude / 'you're just a salesperson'", "response_steps": ["De-escalate and reset the frame: 'I hear you — and I'm genuinely not here to sell you. I'm here to see if this is a fit. If it's not, I'll tell you straight and point you in the right direction.'", "Match-then-lower their energy: stay calm, lower your tone, don't get defensive. Treat it as a puzzle, not a threat.", "Take responsibility if the call slipped: 'That's my bad — I think I got ahead of myself. Let's slow down. The main thing is [their problem] — talk to me about that.'"], "do_not": "Don't argue back or get defensive. A combative prospect is testing whether you'll fold or stay in the lead — stay calm and stay in the lead."}, {"id": "sticker-shock", "button": "Sticker-shock pause", "label": "Pause right after the price — before any named objection", "response_steps": ["Hold the silence. After the price, do not talk first. Let them react.", "If they ask 'how much was that again?' — re-anchor to the outcome, don't just repeat the number: 'The investment to take you from [current] to [outcome] is [price].'", "Then ask the temp check: 'How are you feeling about it?' — and handle whatever objection surfaces."], "do_not": "Don't fill the post-price silence with a softener, a discount, or a payment plan. The first one to talk loses leverage."}, {"id": "emotional", "button": "Got emotional", "label": "Prospect is emotional / vulnerable / opened up", "response_steps": ["Slow down and hold the moment — don't rush to close on top of it: 'I really appreciate you sharing that. That takes guts.'", "Chase it gently: 'Tell me more about that — how's that been showing up for you?'", "Tie it to the decision when the moment settles: 'That right there is exactly why this matters. So let's make sure we fix it.'"], "do_not": "Don't pounce on an emotional moment with a hard close, and don't brush past it. Sit in it, then bridge to the decision."}, {"id": "camera-off", "button": "Camera off", "label": "Prospect joined with camera off -- get it on without being creepy", "response_steps": ["Don't ask 'can you hear me' -- they can. Ask the confused version: 'How well can you hear me? My mic was acting up on the last call.'", "Then act confused about their video: 'Is your video broken? I can't see you.' Forces them to correct the record ('no it's not broken') -- and socially they almost have to turn it on.", "If they admit they always keep it off, go playful: 'Dude, what's going on, it's 12:45 over there -- you still in your pajamas? If I'd known I would have worn my underwear on here.' Playful tone -> they laugh and turn it on."], "do_not": "Don't say 'I want to see who we're working with' -- creepy. Don't say 'is your camera off' -- accusatory, not confused. The whole move is the CONFUSED tonality."}, {"id": "easy-yes-trap", "button": "Too-easy yes", "label": "'This sounds great' / 'I really want to do this' — enthusiastic tone but the BUT is loaded", "response_steps": ["Don't celebrate: 'You know the but's coming.' Enthusiasm + no payment question = pre-objection setup.", "Interject BEFORE the but lands: 'Hold on — why do you feel like you really want to do this?' Forces them to sell themselves on the program in their own words before the objection forms.", "Listen to the TONE of THAT answer. Certainty ('man, I have to do this') → closer to a real yes. Soft ('well, I mean, it sounds good...') → the BUT is still coming, handle it now.", "tell: 'I really want to do this. Where do I pay?' = real. 'This sounds great, I really want to do this...' (trailing) = BUT incoming. Catch it BEFORE they speak the objection into existence — once spoken they have to defend it."], "do_not": "Don't treat enthusiastic-sounding language as a buy signal — the tone tells you whether the next sentence has a BUT. Run the why-loop first."}], "objections": [{"id": "price-too-expensive", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "It's too expensive / I can't afford it / that's a lot of money", "triggers": ["too expensive", "pretty expensive", "can't afford it", "can't afford that", "don't know if I can afford", "how I can afford", "that's a lot of money", "a lot of money for this", "that's just a lot for me right now", "it's just a lot for me right now", "it's too much", "it's too much money", "more than I thought", "out of my budget", "out of budget", "stretch out of budget", "pricey", "don't have the money", "I have no money", "got no money", "can't make this work", "come up with the money", "really struggling", "that's pretty steep", "that's steep", "almost as much as a new car", "got to find the money", "got to see if I can afford it", "no money", "have no money", "no money to", "no money right now", "no budget", "no budget for", "zero budget", "cant afford", "cant afford it", "dont have the money", "dont have money", "dont have it", "dont have the cash", "broke right now", "im broke", "tight on cash", "cash poor", "money is tight", "cant swing it", "cant swing that"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Now, just to stay organized on my end — when you say you can't afford it, are you more in a 'should I do this?' kinda place where you're not even sure this is what you want to do? Or more of a 'how can I do this?' place where you're 100% certain you want to do this, it's just a matter of making it work financially? (This isolates uncertainty smoke-screen vs genuine financial logistic.)", "Gotcha. So if I'm hearing you correctly — money aside, you're 100% in? (Only do the rest of this AFTER you have the double tie-down.)", "Look — most of my clients do the investment up front. But for certain clients in situations where they really want to do it, it's just the money — we break it up. So given you're 100% in and it's really just about finding a way to make it work financially — are you open to exploring the option of that? (This gets permission to go into payment plans. It's why we don't offer payment plans straight away.)", "[They say 'sure, what does it look like?'] Well, that depends — everything is customised based on what you need. So are you open to having an honest conversation financially and putting everything out on the table, so we can see if there's any possibility of doing this now — or at the very least we can create a game plan to work towards this in the future? (Frames the open wallet in their best interest, with permission. Removes sales pressure.)", "OK great. So, in the next 30 days, how much cash flow coming in do you have total?... Gotcha. And after all expenses, how much do you have left coming in in total? (Cash flow — pacing question, less invasive.)", "Sure, cool. And what's your cash on hand exactly right now?... And that's the exact number you have available? (If they give a round number like 12k, real. If they give a specific number like $500, 99% of the time that's a smoke screen — they're telling you what they can spend in this moment, not what they have.)", "And in terms of credit — not saying we have to use it, but just so I have full understanding of how things are looking — what's available to you right now?", "And you really wanna do this, right?", "OK because look — I don't think the best thing for you to do right now is drop [the full price] and invest all your savings on this or go into credit card debt. But I also know that your business is really important to you, and if you don't do something in the next 6-12 months, I also don't think the best thing to do is nothing. And plus, for you, it's what — [N] clients to break even? So because of that, I'd be willing to let you in for [$X] down — get lead gen going, get clients in. Is that fair? So if that's something I'm willing to do for you — is that something you're willing to move forward with right now?"], "do_not": "Do not offer a payment plan as the rebuttal to uncertainty. Cheaper terms never fix belief. Confirm 'money aside, 100% in' FIRST. Then get permission to explore — don't dive into open wallet without it. Never offer payment plans or discounts before the price drop — they're closing leverage.", "alt_reframes": ["Expensive compared to what, though? 5K for a dinner is expensive; 5K for a car is cheap. Does it really matter what we pay if what we get in return is everything you've ever wanted?", "Has 10K always been a lot to you? Do you want it to always be a lot, or do you want to be the kind of person who can move on something that's going to 100% help you? You're never going to get out of the place where 10K is a lot if you make decisions out of your circumstances instead of your vision."], "source": "objections/price-and-financial.md"}, {"id": "think-about-it", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I want to think about it / send me the info / I'll get back to you", "triggers": ["think about it", "need to think about it", "think it over", "think on this", "let me think", "wants to think", "want to think", "really want to think", "pray on it", "pray about it", "send this over", "send it over", "send me the info", "send me everything", "send me a proposal", "send me an email", "all this in an email", "get back to you", "get back to you next week", "I'll let you know", "I need some time", "give me some time", "gather myself", "have all the information", "mull it over", "circle back", "circle back next quarter"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Before we get into any of that — let me ask you this, just because we've been through a lot today. How do you actually feel? Money and everything aside, do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [their goal], and that it's 100% going to work?", "If they waffle ('I think so'): Got it — but what I'm really trying to understand is, do you think this is 100% going to work, and do you 100% want to do this? It doesn't sound 100% certain — so let's just be honest with each other, what's really going on?", "INVERSION: Deliberately mishear the hedge as a no -- 'so it sounds like you don't think it's going to work?' 9/10 they snap back: 'no no, I do think it's going to work.' Lower your tone: 'hold on -- why do you feel like it's going to work?' Now they're selling you on the program in their own words -- closest thing to a self-close. Loop 'why though' on each answer until the real concern surfaces.", "If a real concern surfaces, that's the true objection — handle it (route to the matching entry).", "If it IS a genuine sleep-on-it: No issue at all, I'd sleep on it too if I were you. So just to clarify — if we schedule a time tomorrow and you wake up feeling the exact same way you feel right now, then what you're telling me is we're 100% processing the payment and moving forward, yes?", "Why don't you come in now and draw the line in the sand today — and if you wake up tomorrow and at the bottom of your gut you know it was a terrible decision, we'll just refund you.", "INVERSION CLOSE (after 3-4 layers of 'why though?'): 'Tell me why you getting [their stated outcome] would be the WRONG thing for you.' They literally cannot answer — they'd have to argue against their own goal. Usually they say 'wait, say that again?' Repeat it slow: 'is [outcome] the right thing or the wrong thing?' Either way they concede → 'why?' They sell themselves."], "do_not": "Don't accept a vague 'I'll get back to you' and book a loose follow-up. Desire fades. Isolate now, or lock a next-day call with a definitive tie-down.", "source": "objections/think-about-it.md", "alt_reframes": ["CLOSE THE LOOP (Jeremy Miner / Cole): Most of the weight people carry is from open loops, not closed ones. 'Either it's a yes today and the loop closes, or it's a no today and the loop closes. Booking another call to think about it just keeps the loop open. Which is it?'"]}, {"id": "need-to-do-research", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I need to do research / due diligence", "triggers": ["do some research", "do my research", "need to do research", "due diligence", "look into it", "look you guys up", "I just found out about you", "just found out about you guys", "need to see case studies", "see some reviews", "check you out", "read some reviews"], "response_steps": ["No problem at all, happy for you to do that. Just so I can stay organized and get clarity on my end — what's keeping you from being less than 100% certain that this is going to get you to [their outcome]?", "So basically what I'm understanding is — you 100% think this will work and you want to move forward, you just want to do a little research to confirm everything I told you checks out. As long as it lines up, you're 100% good to go?", "No problem — I can help speed up that research. What specifically do you want to see — reviews, case studies, videos? I can prepare something and send it over.", "If they can't name anything specific: Can I be honest with you for a second? Earlier you said you're 100% certain — but when I ask what you want to find out more about, you say nothing in particular. One of my core values is transparency, so I can't help feeling you're just not that into this, which is okay. What's really going on?"], "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "talk-to-your-clients", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I need to talk to one of your clients", "triggers": ["talk to one of your clients", "speak to one of your clients", "talk to some of your clients", "speak with your clients", "talk to a client", "do you have clients I can speak to", "references", "speak to a reference"], "response_steps": ["Got it — let's cover that in a second. But just for clarity, aside from that, how do you feel? Do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [outcome], and you 100% want to do it?", "So theoretically — if you spoke to one of our clients and they validated everything I've told you so far, you're basically good to go, we're processing payment?", "Here's our policy: we have 100+ people reaching out every month wanting to become clients. It wouldn't be appropriate or realistic to fill our clients' calendars with people who are still just thinking about joining — especially when our clients are wealthy business owners who charge for their time. That's the exact reason we have 500+ case studies. Is there a specific type of case study you were looking for?", "Alternative: If I connect you with a client right after this call, are you 100% okay keeping the exchange to text out of respect for their time?... And once they echo everything I told you and we talk in 48 hours, what do you think the next step is from there?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "spouse-partner", "bucket": "support", "type": "logistic", "label": "I need to talk to my spouse / partner / business partner", "triggers": ["talk to my wife", "talk to my husband", "talk to my spouse", "talk to my partner", "run it by my wife", "run it by my partner", "run it by my husband", "run this by my", "my business partner", "ask my wife", "ask my husband", "let my wife know", "let my husband know", "let my spouse know", "check with my partner", "check with somebody", "check with someone else", "pass it by", "financial advisor", "discuss with my partner", "sync with my partner", "need to talk to somebody else"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Just so I can be clear — talking to your spouse aside, how do you feel for you personally? Do you feel this is 100% what you need to get to [goal], and that it's 100% going to work?", "Cool. So just to clarify — if your spouse was on this call right now and said 'I believe you, do whatever's best for the business,' if they'd already given you that green light, would you be 100% moving forward and processing the payment with me right now?", "Aside from letting your spouse know, is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain this is what you need?", "Just for clarity's sake — is this a respect thing where you've basically decided and you're just letting them know, or do you genuinely need to sit down, collaborate, and get their permission to move forward?", "What do you think they're going to think about this? What will they say when they hear the investment? Are they supportive of you fixing [the problem]? Do they know you're on this call?", "There are two ways you can bring this up. One — 'Honey, that business I spent a ton on, I met a guy on the internet, it's 10k, what do you think?' Or two — you sit them down and confidently say 'I've decided and committed to growing this where it should be, and I found someone to help. I'm not asking permission, I'm asking for your emotional support and buy-in.' Which of those two guys do you think convinces his wife? You're right — and if you're not certain, neither will they be, nor should they be.", "FUTURE-PACE: How does your spouse feel about you losing $[N] a month right now? Is she more stressed about you losing $[N]/month — or about you investing $[X] to fix it?... How many months are we going to keep pushing this off while you keep losing $[N] a month? (Reframes the spouse from blocker to ally via consequence math.)", "Let's put down a refundable deposit now, I'll onboard you, and schedule a call with you, your spouse and me so they can see exactly what you'd be investing in. If they hate it, we refund it. So if I was willing to do that for you, would you be willing to move forward right now?", "EXTERNAL-VALIDATION REFRAME: 'Can I share something? The brain isn't built to thrive, it's built to keep us safe. So when we hit something new, the default is to outsource the decision -- talk to the spouse, the advisor -- so if it doesn't work out, it wasn't our fault. That's not actually about your spouse. That's your brain looking for a way to push this down the road. Real question -- if you take the spouse out of it: do YOU think this works, and do YOU 100% want to do it?'"], "do_not": "Never chase the spouse objection before the prospect themselves is 100% sold. If they're not sold, they cannot sell someone who wasn't on the call.", "source": "objections/support-spouse-partner-team.md"}, {"id": "multiple-partners", "bucket": "support", "type": "logistic", "label": "We need to discuss amongst ourselves (3+ partners / decision-makers)", "triggers": ["discuss amongst ourselves", "discuss with the partners", "talk to the other partners", "the three of us", "all the partners", "discuss internally", "we need to discuss", "let us talk about it", "talk it over together"], "response_steps": ["Go person by person on the temp check: 'Jim, where are you out of 10?... Mark, where are you out of 10?... Alex, looks like you're the only one not certain — it's a two-to-three vote, looks like we're good to go.' You're just closing three people instead of one.", "If you can't close on the call: Your partners weren't on this call, so they won't have all the information, and it's a lot for you to relay. Let's schedule a 30-minute call with all of us where I recap everything and re-show them exactly what it looks like to work with us, and all of us decide together.", "Lock the tie-down: So when we talk tomorrow, after you've spoken — if you feel the same way you told me you feel right now, then we're 100% moving forward, yes or no?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "discuss-with-team", "bucket": "support", "type": "logistic", "label": "I need to run it by my team / board / CFO (downward authority)", "triggers": ["run it by my team", "talk to my team", "check with my team", "run it by the board", "talk to my board", "run it by my CFO", "check with the team", "my team has to implement", "team bandwidth", "compliance team"], "response_steps": ["If you believe this is the number one constraint in your business, your job as the CEO is to determine the problem, the priority, the vision — and align everyone to attack it. You shouldn't be going to your team asking for permission.", "If they say no, are you prepared to tell them, 'Guys, we are doing this'? You're not asking them for permission — you're asking them for buy-in.", "If it's genuinely a bandwidth question: get the implementer on a call, or pre-handle it — 'does your team have the bandwidth to implement this this quarter?'"], "source": "objections/support-spouse-partner-team.md"}, {"id": "been-burned", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I've been burned before / I tried something like this and it didn't work", "triggers": ["been burned", "burned before", "it didn't work", "it didn't work last time", "how is this different", "how is this going to be different", "don't see how this is different", "what we did before", "tried before", "tried something like this", "tried something similar", "bad experience", "got scammed", "wasted money", "wasted my money", "last company didn't fulfill", "overpromised", "I've done this before", "I've seen this before", "skeptical", "paid an agency before"], "response_steps": ["Totally get it, that's super frustrating — a lot of times we're picking up the pieces after someone overpromised and underdelivered.", "Tell me what happened in that company — what was the difference between what you thought would happen and what was actually implemented?", "What we've found, doing this with thousands of clients, is it comes down to one of three things: number one, the process they implemented just didn't work; number two, the strategy was good but the service wasn't — slow, no support; or number three, both were fine and you just didn't show up the way you should have. Which one of those do you think it was?", "[They name it — usually method or service] So given the service quality is the same, if the method is right, wouldn't it make sense you wouldn't get the same result as before? So with that out of the way — do you really think this is going to work?", "You learned the lesson 'don't work with a beginner' — don't learn the wrong lesson and make it 'this type of thing never works.' That one bad decision is just the tuition you paid to make a better, more informed decision this time. Let's not let one bad decision sabotage a great one.", "RE-MEANING: 'You know what's interesting about that? That bad experience didn't break you -- it led you here. Most people would have quit and gone back to a job. You didn't.' Changing the MEANING of the failure from 'evidence this never works' to 'evidence you're built for this.' Re-meaning FIRST, identity-shift SECOND -- doing identity without re-meaning sounds like a glib compliment.", "IDENTITY-SHIFT: Sounds like you're the type of entrepreneur who never gives up — you tried [X], it didn't work, and you're still here trying to find a real solution. So why is this so important to you?... Were you born that way, or did you have to learn it? (Locks the new identity — they can't object without contradicting their new self-image.)", "If comparing to a small past provider: You're comparing a 3-person shop with 5 clients and no sales team to a category leader with 3,000+ clients and an 8-figure sales team. How does that comparison even make sense?", "EGO-STATE TIE: To a male prospect: 'and your spouse — she's lucky to have a provider like you, someone forward-thinking who makes the hard decisions for the family.' To a female prospect: 'and your spouse — he's lucky to have an independent woman like you who [their move].' Plays to ego state (provider for males, independence for females). Locks the new identity through a witness they care about. ADAPT to what the prospect actually values — some male prospects value being seen as an equal partner over provider; read the signal, don't default-stereotype."], "do_not": "Don't argue them out of the feeling with a glib analogy ('would you never date again?'). Diagnose what actually happened, then separate it from your offer.", "source": "objections/been-burned-before.md"}, {"id": "competitor-cheaper", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Your competitor is cheaper / I'm shopping around / talking to other people", "triggers": ["competitor", "cheaper", "cheaper option", "other option", "other quotes", "get a couple quotes", "shopping around", "other companies", "talking to other", "go with someone else", "talking to someone else", "another program", "another guy", "talked to a guy", "yours is more", "5k cheaper", "looking into other", "looking into a couple", "we're talking to three other guys"], "response_steps": ["Quick question before anything else — are you looking for the cheapest option, or are you looking for the team that's most likely to get you there?", "Curious — how are you thinking about this? What held you back from going with the other ones?", "Ultimately, how would you know if you'd found the right team to help you?... So it's really just about who's going to get you where you want to go, right? Aside from evaluating which option to go with, it sounds like you're going to do something — it's just a matter of who. So let's take price aside for a moment: out of the two options, which are you more certain can actually get you there?", "Can I just be your bro for a sec? You're doing [X], you want to get to [Y]. Whether the investment is five grand or fifty relative to that goal — who gives a damn? Go with the team that's done what you want to do the most amount of times and that you're most sure can get you there.", "If the other option is genuinely solid, sequence it instead of trashing it: come work with us first to get the foundation right, and if you still want to, go work with that guy in three months. And just so you know what to watch for — a team that won't even let you go talk to other programs first, that's a red flag.", "WHAT THEY'LL SAY: What are you hoping that other company is going to say?... Do you think they're going to say they're worse than us? Of course not — every salesperson says they're the best. So what's that really telling you?", "INTUITION CLOSE: Let's say their proposal looks similar to ours and the price is similar. How would you actually decide who to go with?... Your intuition? OK — what does your intuition say right now?... Why?", "DELIVERY: As you contrast their option vs yours, physically separate your hands -- their option here, your option there. Even on audio the gesture changes your tone enough for the prospect to feel the split. Sitting still flattens the frame. 'Selling from stage they point to the doors -- same thing on a phone.'", "BINARY FORCE: 'Is the cheapest price the most important thing to you, or actually like scaling your company to $[goal]?' Force the binary — they can't logically pick 'cheapest.' Then anchor the ROI ratio: 'Because whether it's 10K or 20K, the result is 10x that either way if it works.' Collapses 'shopping' from price-comparison frame into outcome-comparison."], "do_not": "Don't trash the competitor — bulldozing makes you look like 'just a closer.' Educate on the options instead. If a competitor is genuinely solid, sequence it: 'come work with us first, then go work with that guy in 3 months.'", "source": "objections/competitor-cheaper.md"}, {"id": "timing-start-later", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I want to start later / after the holidays / next quarter / after my trip", "triggers": ["start later", "after the holidays", "after the new year", "start next quarter", "next quarter initiative", "wait till next quarter", "circle back in three months", "start next month", "do it next month", "wait till next month", "not right now", "bad timing", "start january", "after my vacation", "after my trip", "after the wedding", "want to do it in two months", "start in two weeks"], "response_steps": ["Got it. So timing aside — you're 100% in?", "Just to be clear — if we're having this exact conversation on [their start date] and you feel the same way, you're 100% giving me your credit card and moving forward?", "Well, I've got an idea — are you open to it? I don't think the best thing for you is to wait and do nothing. But I also don't think the best thing is to hop in when you can't fully commit. So what I'd be willing to do is add 30 days onto your engagement — you start now, knock out the onboarding, and when your official start date comes we hit the ground running. So if I was willing to do that for you, would you be willing to move forward right now?", "If it's a trip: honestly the timing's perfect — on a long flight you'll have time to knock out the onboarding and training you wouldn't have working full-time. I'll set your official start date for [date] and buy you extra time in the program."], "source": "objections/timing-start-later.md"}, {"id": "no-time-to-implement", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I don't have time to implement this right now", "triggers": ["don't have time", "no time", "don't have the time", "too busy", "no time to implement", "can't dedicate the time", "can't dedicate any time", "able to dedicate", "swamped", "no bandwidth", "stretched thin", "wearing all the hats", "too much on my plate"], "response_steps": ["No problem. So timing aside — is there anything else keeping you from being less than 100% certain?", "Can I tell you what I'm seeing? You told me the number one problem in your business is [their constraint]. And your bottleneck to solving it is time. But the reason you don't have time IS [the constraint]. So the very problem you got on this call to solve is the exact thing keeping you from getting started — you're in a self-perpetuating loop, you're stuck.", "So the real problem isn't time, it's a mix-up of priorities. You've already identified [the constraint] as the problem and this as the best way to fix it — so isn't this your number one priority?", "I'm not asking you to work more hours — I'm asking you to direct the hours you already have into the number one constraint in your business. If you're going to grow it, why would you not focus on this now? If not now, when?", "You make time to go to the gym and be healthy — it's not a question. What you really need is one to two hours a day. Is it genuinely impossible for you to wake up an hour earlier or go to bed an hour later?"], "source": "objections/timing-start-later.md"}, {"id": "nerves-fear", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Nerves / fear — they're 100% in but freeze, or it's 'a big decision'", "triggers": ["nervous", "scared", "nerves", "anxious", "hesitant", "cold feet", "freaking out", "it's a big decision", "big decision", "can't pull the trigger", "it's just hard to decide", "hard for me to make a decision", "hard to make a decision", "this is a lot to take in", "it's just a lot", "scary"], "response_steps": ["Release the pressure: Can I ask you a personal question? There's probably something else going through your head. We've been talking a while, and from my end everything about this makes sense for you. Will you just open up and tell me what you're thinking — what's really going on?", "Name it: It just seems like it's a little bit of nerves. Is it?... Good — the nerves are good. That means there's weight to this, there's meaning to it. I'd think you were an alien if you weren't a little nervous. Nothing great in the world was ever built by someone who wasn't a little nervous at first.", "Identity: So the nerves are really irrelevant here. The real question is — who do you want to be? The type of person who feels the fear and does it anyway, or the type who lets nervousness make the decision? Which is it?", "Can I ask you a weird question — does it feel like your head and your heart are playing tug-of-war? Your brain is trying to keep you safe, it's yelling at you not to do it — but your heart is the thing that lit up when you told me what [outcome] would mean. Which one do you think will take you farther?", "There are two parts to your brain — the monkey brain that keeps you safe, and the part that wants you to succeed. How many people do you know who knew about Bitcoin in 2010 and did nothing? They listened to the monkey brain. Listen to the part that's going to make you successful."], "source": "objections/nerves-cant-pull-trigger.md"}, {"id": "what-if-it-doesnt-work", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "What if it doesn't work for me / I don't think it'll work", "triggers": ["what if it doesn't work", "doesn't work for me", "won't work for me", "don't think it'll work", "not sure it'll work", "afraid it won't work", "I'll be the one it doesn't work for", "how do I know this works", "what if I'm the exception"], "response_steps": ["Just so I can stay organized — what you're saying is, despite the hundreds of case studies and the [X]% success rate, you're worried you'll be the small percentage this doesn't work for, right?", "Can I ask you an honest question? If you come in and do this — number one, are you 100% going to put in the work? And number two, when you hit a snag, are you going to raise your hand and ask for help, or bury your head in the sand?", "So if we have a 90%+ success rate for people who do the work, and you're 100% going to put in the work, and you promise you'll raise your hand when you need help — then tell me, why wouldn't this work for you?", "If I hand you the best camping gear with a big guarantee on it — who still has to fill the canteen with water and walk the trail? You. So the real question isn't about the program — it's whether you're committed to being the person who gets the result from it."], "source": "objections/been-burned-before.md"}, {"id": "is-there-a-guarantee", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Is there a guarantee?", "triggers": ["is there a guarantee", "do you have a guarantee", "can you guarantee", "guaranteed results", "what's the guarantee", "money back guarantee"], "response_steps": ["We can definitely talk about that. Just curious — is there a specific reason you're asking? (This sniffs out the hidden objection behind it — usually 'I've been burned.')", "Honestly, there's a lot that's out of our control — like, are you going to put in the work? Me guaranteeing a specific result would be illegal, immoral and unethical anyway. What I CAN guarantee is that we'll give you every tool and resource you need to get [the outcome], and that we have an impeccable track record.", "What really matters is two things: are you going to 100% show up and do the work, and when you hit a problem — which you will — are you going to raise your hand for help?... Great question, what else?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "too-risky", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "It's too risky / too big a risk / too good to be true", "triggers": ["too risky", "it's a risk", "it's risky", "feels risky", "big risk", "too big of a risk", "too good to be true", "sounds too good", "big leap"], "response_steps": ["I hear you on that. Can I give you a little coaching on it?... Your goal is to make [X] a year — that would put you in the top 1%. Have you ever wondered why so few people make that kind of money despite wanting it? It's the fear of risk.", "So the real question isn't 'is this too risky' — the real question is who do you want to be? When 99% of people bump into that glass wall of fear and risk, they contract and retreat to their comfort zone — which is exactly what keeps them where they are. The 1% feel the fear and break through.", "So which of those two people do you want to be?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "do-it-myself", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I'll just do it myself / try it on my own first", "triggers": ["do it myself", "do this myself", "do it on my own", "try it myself", "try it on my own first", "figure it out myself", "I can do this", "I'll just try it and see"], "response_steps": ["Use their own words against the objection: 'Wait — earlier on the call you told me [what they said about being stuck / having tried]. Now you're saying you'll do it on your own. What's really going on?'", "You've been trying to figure this out for [time] — I'm not saying you can't do it, you likely have every capability you need. So the question isn't can you or can't you. The question is: what's the fastest, most probable path that stacks everything in your favor?", "Curse-of-knowledge reframe (for agency/expert prospects): The classic saying is 'I'm great at getting results for my clients but not for myself.' That's not your fault — it's just the curse of knowledge. If I were you, I'd hedge the bet the most in my favor.", "Why would you want to use a proven pathway? Because it requires less mental and financial resources to get there faster than figuring it out alone."], "source": "objections/00-core-framework.md"}, {"id": "want-to-see-it", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "It sounds good but I need to see it first", "triggers": ["need to see it", "want to see it", "see it first", "show me", "see how it works", "see the inside", "see the platform", "don't know until I see it"], "response_steps": ["That's totally fine. Help me understand — when you say 'see it,' what exactly are you looking to see, just so I can help?", "Yeah, no worries — let me share my screen right now. I'll walk you through the training portal and give you a glimpse inside the community so you can see exactly what it looks like to be a client.", "(Note: 'I need to see it' usually means they just can't picture what working with you looks like — so show them.)"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "same-day-decisions", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I never make same-day decisions / I always sleep on big decisions", "triggers": ["never make same-day decisions", "don't decide same day", "always sleep on", "personal rule", "I have a rule", "don't make decisions on the first call", "need 24 hours", "rule where I wait", "I never decide same day"], "response_steps": ["Can I tell you what I think we should do? Let's put down a refundable deposit — I'll fully onboard you, and if at any moment what I told you we'd deliver isn't in alignment with what you're getting, I'll give you a 100% refund, because we didn't uphold our end. So it's a no-risk decision.", "Help me understand — if it's a no-risk decision and you're a 10 out of 10, what would hold you back from just moving forward?", "The way you've made decisions in the past created the results you have now — the exact results you're on this call to change. To change them, we have to change the pattern of how you make decisions.", "You said you want to make an informed decision — but the only informed decision you can make is from the inside, actually seeing the product. Are you more informed from the inside or the outside?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "trust-why-you", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Why should I trust you / how do I know you're legit", "triggers": ["why should I trust you", "how do I know", "are you legit", "is this a scam", "trust you", "why is it you I should trust", "how do I know this is real", "you could be anyone"], "response_steps": ["B2C: [Name], totally hear you. Here's what I'm going to do — I'm sending you a text right now. Did you get it? Great, that's my personal cell. When I say I care about your success, I mean it — any time you're a client, if you need anything, text or call me. I've got your back, I'm not going to let you fail.", "B2B: [Big-name clients] trusted us. Do you think they don't know how to make good buying decisions? Of course they do. You should trust this too.", "Reframe the rep's own mindset: if prospects keep feeling 'untrustworthy of you,' you may be pushing too hard and making them defensive. Lead supportive, not combative."], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "payment-plan", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "Do you have a payment plan? / Can we break it into payments?", "triggers": ["payment plan", "break it up", "break it into payments", "break it into two", "split it up", "monthly payments", "can I pay monthly", "instalments", "can we do a two pay", "can I do a 10 pay", "finance it"], "response_steps": ["Don't just give it. First confirm: 'When you're on a call and a client has the money, needs it, and knows they need it — do you think they should break it into two?... So money aside, you're 100% in?'", "Run the open wallet (30-day cash → cash on hand exactly → credit) to find the biggest plan they can comfortably and ethically do.", "Then trade the concession for a decision: 'I don't think the best thing for you is to drain your savings, but I also don't think the best thing is to do nothing. So what I'd be willing to do is let you in for [half] down — and if I'm willing to do that for you, are you willing to move forward right now?'", "If you have to go lower again, ask for more back: 'If I'm willing to do that for you, will you move forward right now AND give me a case study when you get amazing results?'"], "do_not": "Never blurt 'what about a two-pay?' or hand over a plan free. A concession with no exchange has no value. Always trade it for a decision.", "source": "objections/price-and-financial.md"}, {"id": "move-money-around", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "I'm 100% in, I just need to move money around / wait for a payment", "triggers": ["move money around", "move some money", "move funds", "transfer funds", "organize my funds", "organize funds", "free up some money", "wait for a client payment", "waiting on a payment", "buying a house", "give me two days", "give me till friday", "pay in full in a couple days", "money's tied up"], "response_steps": ["Okay, walk me through it real fast so I can stay organized. When you say you're moving money around — what does that look like? Where's it coming from? Selling stocks, a 401k, a brokerage account?", "And when is that going to be finished?... And once it's done, you're 100% moving forward that day?", "Then let's do the bulk of it now — say seven-and-a-half of the ten — that way we still get you onboarded, get the assessment, get the forms and the onboarding call out of the way, and we just take care of the rest in a week when you're done moving the money around. (You're already 100% in and the money is real — take most of it now, not half.)", "Gentleman's agreement: Let's get this done now so you get access to everything and knock out the onboarding forms — just make me a gentleman's agreement that you'll have the rest down before your onboarding call."], "source": "objections/timing-start-later.md"}, {"id": "make-money-first", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Let me make some money first, then I'll buy", "triggers": ["make money first", "once I make some money", "after I get some results", "after I land a client", "make some sales first", "get some income first", "do this other thing first then come back"], "response_steps": ["Can I be really honest? If you had the winning lottery ticket, don't you think you'd have cashed it in by now? If you had the ability to change your situation and make more money, you'd have done it already — and we wouldn't be on this phone. Do you agree?", "If you had all the tools you needed to change [their circumstance], you would have already changed it. So waiting to 'make money first' is waiting for the exact thing this is designed to fix."], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "not-allowed-coaching", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I'm not allowed to / not interested in buying a coaching program", "triggers": ["not allowed to buy", "not interested in coaching", "can't buy a coaching program", "not allowed to purchase", "just an informal call", "not looking to buy anything"], "response_steps": ["Based on what we covered, we can definitely help. I know you said you're not interested in a coaching program — but you just told me [what they said they want / their pain], and I know we can help you get [core desired result], because we've done it for [case study, case study, case study].", "So if you're open, I can walk you through what the program is and how it helps you — but I want this to be a serious conversation where you're actually considering it, otherwise we're both wasting our time. So where do you want to go from here?"], "source": "objections/more-objections-from-webinar.md"}, {"id": "prospect-taking-control", "bucket": "process", "type": "process", "label": "Just get to the price / just tell me what you've got (prospect taking control)", "triggers": ["just tell me what you got", "get to the price", "what's the price", "just give me the price", "skip to the point", "I get sold all the time", "let me ask my questions", "how much is it", "just tell me how it works"], "response_steps": ["I'm totally prepared to share what we have going on and how we might help if it makes sense. But everything we do is customized — so at this stage what makes the most sense is let me get a little context on your business: your market, how you're generating leads now, what's going on with your team. Then I can share the parts of what we do that are relevant and useful to you specifically. That's the most time-efficient way — is that cool?", "Take responsibility for the conversation if it slipped: 'Oh, I totally apologize, I think I misheard something — that's my bad. So the main thing is [their problem] — how are you currently [doing the thing] right now?'", "Match their energy: if they're super direct, be super direct back. Stay calm, stay in the lead, treat it as a fun puzzle, not a threat."], "source": "sales-process/01-introduction-and-discovery.md"}, {"id": "waffling-smokescreen", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Prospect is waffling / won't name a concern / 'I think so'", "triggers": ["I think so", "I guess so", "I don't know", "I'm not sure", "I wouldn't say 100", "it's just a lot to think about", "I just need to process this"], "response_steps": ["Cut in playfully and call out the tonality: 'I think so? That doesn't sound 100% certain — so let's just be honest with each other for a second, what's really going on?'", "Man, can I ask you a personal question? There's probably something else going through your head. From my end everything about this makes sense for you. Will you just open up and tell me what you're thinking?", "Just level with me — what's really going on? Earlier you said you wanted to do this, you said it sounds really good. If you do it now or later that's fine, but it feels like something's on your mind we haven't discussed. If we're going to work together, we have to be honest with each other. So what's really going on?", "Feed them the objection if they still can't name it: 'It just sounds like it's a little bit of nerves — is it?' Then handle nerves."], "do_not": "Don't let a vague 'I think so' slide into a booked follow-up. Turn the intangible into a tangible objection you can actually handle.", "source": "objections/00-core-framework.md"}, {"id": "discount-request", "bucket": "financial", "type": "logistic", "label": "Are you offering any discounts?", "triggers": ["discount", "any discounts", "can you do better on price", "do anything on the price", "best you can do", "any deals", "anything cheaper", "knock the price down", "lower the price", "best price"], "response_steps": ["No. (There's nothing more you need to say than that. Don't do fast-action discounts or incentive-based pricing — they're a closing crutch and they cheapen the offer.)", "Quote the price as a flat statement and then go silent — 'the investment to get your business to [outcome] is just [price].' Do not fill the pause with a softener or a payment plan. Let the silence sit.", "If pressed, redirect to value, never to price: re-anchor the price to the outcome, and ask the binary — 'are you looking for the cheapest option, or a premium-quality option?' Keep the investment simple and fixed; payment terms (not discounts) are the only lever, and only after isolating a true financial objection."], "source": "objections/price-and-financial.md"}, {"id": "send-me-recording", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Send me the recording / a summary / email me and I'll review it", "triggers": ["send me the recording", "send the recording", "send me a summary", "email me the", "send me a recap", "send over the recording", "I'll review it", "review it on my own time", "go over it later"], "response_steps": ["No problem. Before I do that — let me ask you this: money and everything aside, do you feel like this is 100% what you need to get to [their goal], and that it's 100% going to work?", "Here's what I've found — a recording without me there to answer the questions that come up usually just sits there. So let's not let that happen to you. What's the real thing you'd be reviewing for — is there something specific you're still not sure about?", "If a real concern surfaces, that's the true objection — handle it. If there isn't one, don't book a loose follow-up: 'It sounds like you're 100% there. Let's just get you started — what's your billing address?'", "If they genuinely need a hard next step: lock a specific time tomorrow with a definitive tie-down — 'when we talk at [time], if you feel the same way, we're 100% moving forward, yes?'"], "do_not": "Don't treat this like 'think about it' and isolate certainty for ten minutes — and don't just send a recording into the void. This is the post-call-disappearance setup. Either close now or lock a hard, tied-down next step.", "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "flat-exit", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "I'll get back to you — flat exit / hand on the doorknob", "triggers": ["I'll get back to you", "let me get back to you", "I'll be in touch", "I'll reach out", "we'll let you know", "leave it with me", "I'll think it through and let you know"], "response_steps": ["Read the tonality. If they've clearly already decided and are just being polite, don't run another temp-check loop — use the honest takeaway.", "TAKEAWAY: 'Can I be totally straight with you? It feels like this is a no — and that's completely okay, I'd rather you tell me than disappear. Be honest with me: it's a no, isn't it?'", "This usually does one of two things — it either gets a real 'yes it's a no' (so you can ask the one question that surfaces the real reason: 'fair enough — what was the thing that didn't land?'), or it snaps them back: 'no, no, it's not that...' — and now the real objection is on the table.", "Whatever they name, handle it through diffuse -> isolate. Do not accept a vague exit."], "do_not": "Don't book a polite follow-up call you both know won't happen. A flat 'I'll get back to you' is a no being delivered gently — call it, with respect, so you get a real answer.", "source": "objections/think-about-it.md"}, {"id": "buyers-remorse", "bucket": "uncertainty", "type": "true-objection", "label": "Post-close cold feet / can I cancel / I'm not sure I should have done this", "triggers": ["can I cancel", "I want to cancel", "I changed my mind", "not sure I should have", "having second thoughts", "did I make the right", "want a refund", "regret this", "cold feet now"], "response_steps": ["Diffuse and stay calm — do not panic or get defensive: 'Totally hear you, and I'm glad you told me instead of sitting on it. Talk to me — what came up?'", "Re-anchor to why they bought: 'Earlier you told me [their goal / their pain] and that this was exactly what you needed. None of that changed in the last ten minutes — so what's actually going on right now?'", "Name it as nerves if that's what it is: 'This is the monkey brain doing its job — the moment after a big decision is when fear shouts loudest. That doesn't mean it was the wrong decision.'", "Re-confirm the decision and move them into action fast: 'Let's get you into onboarding right now and book your first call — momentum is what kills the doubt. You good?'"], "do_not": "Don't ignore post-close remorse hoping it passes, and don't immediately offer the refund. The deal isn't safe until cash clears and onboarding starts — reassure, re-anchor, and move them into action.", "source": "sales-process/03-committing-phase-and-closes.md"}]}};
